### thing-service — example requests
# thing/thing-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: same as place — {"success","data","error"} with data/error
# OMITTED (not null) on the unused side (#[serde(skip_serializing_if)]).
# Gated by THING_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off).
#
# GOTCHA (curl-verified, same as place): Thing has NO #[serde(default)],
# so create/match/check-duplicates need the full struct — every Vec
# field as [], plus id/created_at/updated_at/is_deleted. The client id
# is kept verbatim (never replaced), so reusing a nil id across two
# creates will 500 on the second.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8084
@thingId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token (curl-verified 401
# "missing authorization header" with none, regardless of
# THING_REQUIRE_AUTH — see person.http for the same pattern).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a thing — the full struct (see the GOTCHA note above).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "id": "{{thingId}}",
  "name": "Pride and Prejudice",
  "alternate_names": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "images": [],
  "same_as": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Get the created thing back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}


### Update a thing (same full-struct requirement as create)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{thingId}}",
  "name": "Pride and Prejudice (annotated edition)",
  "alternate_names": ["P&P"],
  "identifiers": [],
  "images": [],
  "same_as": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Search things
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/search?q=Pride&limit=10


### Probabilistic + deterministic match — also needs the full struct.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "Pride and Prejudice",
  "alternate_names": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "images": [],
  "same_as": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Explicit duplicate check (same full-struct body as match)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "Pride and Prejudice",
  "alternate_names": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "images": [],
  "same_as": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Batch deduplicate — scans the whole index
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things/deduplicate


### Review queue — list pending candidate pairs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/review-queue?status=pending


### Review queue — decide a pending item
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things/review-queue/{{reviewId}}/decision
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "status": "confirmed" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate things (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/things/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{thingId}}", "duplicate_id": "<other-uuid>" }


### Masked view
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}/audit


### FHIR R5 — read this thing as a Device resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Device/{{thingId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a thing
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/things/{{thingId}}
